@@ -40,7 +40,15 @@ rentals.book({ itemId: 'board-1', start: '2026-07-01T00:00:00Z', end: '2026-07-0
   without an hourly price. `book` also throws when the item is already booked for any part of the period.
 - Booking ids are sequential within a service (`booking-1`, `booking-2`, ...), so the same calls always
   give the same ids.
-- Cancellation is not implemented yet.
+- `cancel(bookingId, at)` cancels a booking at the UTC time `at` (e.g. `2026-06-30T18:45:30Z`) and returns
+  `{ bookingId, refund }`, where `refund` is the amount in euro cents given back to the customer. A cancelled
+  booking no longer holds its equipment, so it can be booked again and it stops counting in `availability`.
+  - A cancellation made before the rental starts refunds the full booking total, including the long-rental
+    reduction.
+  - A cancellation made at or after the start of the rental refunds nothing.
+  - A booking can only be cancelled once. `cancel` throws for an unknown or already cancelled booking, or for
+    an `at` that is not a UTC time.
+  - Booking ids are never reused, so a cancelled id stays unambiguous.
 
 Run the tests with `npm test`. The tests run on the TypeScript source directly with Node's built-in
 type stripping (Node 22.18 or later), so no build step or dependency is needed.
